.TH AGENTTRACE 1 "2026-09-03" "agentdfir 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agenttrace \- forensic reconstruction for AI-agent security incidents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agenttrace
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIEVIDENCE_FILES\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agenttrace
is a local-first digital forensics and incident response (DFIR) tool for AI
agents and LLM applications. It ingests already-recorded evidence, verifies
integrity and chain of custody, reconstructs the causal attack chain, detects
attack patterns mapped to MITRE ATLAS, and produces reports (JSON, Markdown,
offline HTML). It is deterministic and runs fully offline.
.PP
Use only on evidence you are authorized to investigate. It is a defensive tool
and has no capability to attack or access remote systems.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ingest
Normalize evidence into unified forensic events (JSON).
.TP
.B verify
Verify integrity and chain of custody; produce a signed manifest.
.TP
.B reconstruct
Build the timeline and causal graph.
.TP
.B detect
Detect attack patterns (mapped to MITRE ATLAS).
.TP
.B report
Produce a JSON / Markdown / self-contained HTML report.
.TP
.B export
Write a portable, signed .tar case bundle.
.TP
.B verify\-bundle
Verify a portable case bundle's integrity and signature.
.TP
.B custody
Print and verify a bundle's chain-of-custody ledger.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-signing\-key \fISTR\fR
HMAC key used to seal/verify the manifest and bundles.
.TP
.B \-\-case\-number \fISTR\fR, \-\-case\-officer \fISTR\fR
Case metadata recorded in the chain-of-custody ledger.
.TP
.B \-\-collector \fINAME\fR
Force a specific evidence collector instead of auto-detection.
.TP
.B \-\-json\-out / \-\-md\-out / \-\-html\-out \fIPATH\fR
Write the report to files (report command).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Detect attack patterns in a set of logs:
.B agenttrace detect logs/*.json logs/*.jsonl
.TP
Produce a full signed report:
.B agenttrace report logs/*.json \-\-signing\-key KEY \-\-html\-out report.html
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/rakshanex/agenttrace
